===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{examples|examples=
* ''John’s milk'' — ''John’s'' is in the genitive (and in the [[possessive case|possessive]]) case.
* ''glass of milk'' — ''milk'' is in the genitive (but not in the possessive) case.
}}

# {{lb|en|grammar}} The [[grammatical case]], chiefly [[applicable]] to [[noun#Noun|nouns]], [[use#Verb|used]] to [[express#Verb|express]] a [[relationship]] of [[origin]] or [[possession]]. It [[correspond]]s [[roughly]] to the [[English#Adjective|English]] [[preposition#Noun|preposition]] {{m|en|of}} and the [[suffix#Noun|suffix]] {{m|en|-'s}}.
#: {{synonyms|en|genitive}}
#* {{RQ:Withycombe Christian Names|edition=1st|chapter=Introduction|page=xiv|passage=In very early times a man seems to have been known by a single name together with his father's name in the '''genitive case''', e.g. ''Marcus Marci''; {{...}}}}

